  <section id="translation-notes">
    <h2>Translation notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The Arabic has small typing slips that I have silently read through,
        such as <span lang="ar" dir="rtl">لينا ل</span> for
        <span lang="ar" dir="rtl">لينال</span> (“to obtain”) and a stray closing
        quote mark after the Sorbonne.
      </li>
      <li>
        “Notable figures and dignitaries” renders
        <span lang="ar" dir="rtl">أعلام … وأعيانهم</span>. The two words are close
        in sense, with the second suggesting men of local standing.
      </li>
      <li>
        “Specialization diploma” and “higher certificate” are literal. The
        Arabic doesn’t say what level of degree was meant.
      </li>
    </ul>
